N00B_DIAG(VALUE_TYPE_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0500", ERROR,
    "a value does not have the type its destination requires",
    "A value stored in a variable, field, element or parameter, or returned\n"
    "from a function, must have the type declared for that destination.\n"
    "Convert the value, or change the declared type:\n"
    "    let x: int = 5\n"
    "    let s: string = \"5\"")
N00B_DIAG(WRITE_THROUGH_READ_ONLY, "N00B-T0501", ERROR,
    "a write reaches through a view parameter or a constant",
    "Nothing reachable from a `view` parameter or a constant may be\n"
    "modified. Declare the parameter `modify` (or the value `var`) when the\n"
    "function needs to write through it:\n"
    "    func bump(modify c: Counter) { c.count = c.count + 1 }")
N00B_DIAG(TYPE_VARIABLE_OUTSIDE_SIGNATURE, "N00B-T0502", ERROR,
    "a type variable appears outside any generic declaration",
    "A type variable such as 'T is introduced by the signature of a\n"
    "function or by a generic record, variant or trait declaration, and is\n"
    "only meaningful inside it. Outside one, use a concrete type:\n"
    "    func first(items: List['T]) -> 'T { return items[0] }")
N00B_DIAG(ATOMIC_FIELD_UPDATE, "N00B-T0503", ERROR,
    "a field of an atomic value is assigned on its own",
    "An atomic value is read and written as a whole, so a single field\n"
    "cannot be updated in place. Build the new value and assign all of it.")
N00B_DIAG(ASSIGN_TO_TYPE_PARAMETER, "N00B-T0504", ERROR,
    "a concrete value is assigned to a place whose type is a type parameter",
    "Inside a generic function, a place typed 'T can hold any type the\n"
    "caller chooses, so a value of one particular type cannot be stored\n"
    "there. Only values of type 'T, such as other parameters, can be.")
N00B_DIAG(ENUM_VALUE_NOT_INTEGER, "N00B-T0505", ERROR,
    "an enum item is given a value that is not an integer literal",
    "Enum item values are written as decimal or hexadecimal integer\n"
    "literals:\n"
    "    enum Color { Red = 1, Green = 0x2 }")
N00B_DIAG(FLAGSET_EMPTY, "N00B-T0506", ERROR,
    "a flagset declares no primitive flags",
    "A flagset needs at least one flag declared by name; combinations are\n"
    "built from those flags:\n"
    "    flagset Mode { Read, Write, Both = Read + Write }")
N00B_DIAG(FLAGSET_UNKNOWN_FLAG, "N00B-T0507", ERROR,
    "a flagset combination names a flag that is not declared before it",
    "A combination may only use flags declared earlier in the same\n"
    "flagset. Declare the flag first, or move the combination after it.")
N00B_DIAG(FLAGSET_TOO_MANY_FLAGS, "N00B-T0508", ERROR,
    "a flagset declares more than 128 primitive flags",
    "A flagset holds at most 128 primitive flags. Split the flags across\n"
    "several flagsets.")
N00B_DIAG(FLAGSET_DUPLICATE_VALUE, "N00B-T0509", ERROR,
    "two members of a flagset have the same value",
    "Every flag and combination in a flagset must have a distinct value.\n"
    "Remove the duplicate or give it a different combination.")
N00B_DIAG(CONTAINER_LITERAL_UNTYPED, "N00B-T0510", ERROR,
    "the item type of a container literal cannot be inferred",
    "An empty list, dict or set literal says nothing about the type of its\n"
    "items. Give the variable a type:\n"
    "    let names: List[string] = []")
N00B_DIAG(LITERAL_MODIFIER_PAYLOAD, "N00B-T0511", ERROR,
    "a literal modifier does not accept the literal it follows",
    "Each literal modifier handles particular kinds of literal, such as\n"
    "strings or lists. Use a literal of a kind the modifier accepts, or a\n"
    "different modifier.")
N00B_DIAG(LITERAL_MODIFIER_NOT_ON_LITERAL, "N00B-T0512", ERROR,
    "a literal modifier follows something that is not a literal",
    "A literal modifier is written directly after a literal, such as\n"
    "\"text\"'r or [1, 2]'set. It cannot follow a name or a parenthesized\n"
    "expression.")
N00B_DIAG(TYPE_DECLARATION_FORM, "N00B-T0513", ERROR,
    "a type is declared with `type` instead of `record` or `object`",
    "Use `record` for a value that is copied on assignment and `object` for\n"
    "a value that is shared:\n"
    "    record Point { x: int; y: int }")
N00B_DIAG(SWITCH_CASE_SUBJECT_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0514", ERROR,
    "switch cases name variant arms of a type the subject does not have",
    "The cases of a switch over a variant must name arms of the subject's\n"
    "own variant type. Switch on a value of that variant type, or name the\n"
    "arms of the subject's type.")
N00B_DIAG(DUPLICATE_DECLARATION, "N00B-N0501", ERROR,
    "a name is declared twice in the same scope",
    "Each name can be declared once per scope. Rename one declaration, or\n"
    "assign to the existing variable instead of declaring it again:\n"
    "    var x = 1\n"
    "    x = 2")
N00B_DIAG(SHADOW_USED_LET, "N00B-N0502", ERROR,
    "a nested declaration hides an outer `let` that the block already used",
    "Inside one block a name must mean one thing. When a block has already\n"
    "used an outer `let` binding, it cannot declare a new binding with the\n"
    "same name later. Give the inner binding a different name.")
N00B_DIAG(SHADOW_LET, "N00B-N0503", WARNING,
    "a nested declaration hides an outer `let` binding",
    "Reusing the name of an outer `let` binding makes the outer value\n"
    "unreachable for the rest of the block, which is easy to misread. Give\n"
    "the inner binding a different name.")
N00B_DIAG(OPAQUE_TYPE_FIELD, "N00B-N0505", ERROR,
    "a field of a type whose fields are hidden is used outside its module",
    "A module can export a type without its fields. Outside that module the\n"
    "type's fields cannot be read or written; use the functions the module\n"
    "exports for it.")
N00B_DIAG(TYPE_NAME_IS_VALUE, "N00B-N0507", ERROR,
    "a type and a value in the same scope have the same name",
    "Types and values share one set of names in a scope, so a type cannot\n"
    "have the name of a variable or function declared beside it. Rename\n"
    "one of them.")
N00B_DIAG(PACKAGE_BLOCK_STATEMENT, "N00B-N0509", ERROR,
    "a package block contains a statement other than `export` or `when`",
    "A `package` block lists what the package exports, optionally under\n"
    "`when` conditions. Imports and other statements go before the block.")
N00B_DIAG(REDUNDANT_PRIVATE, "N00B-N0510", ERROR,
    "a field inside a `private` block is also marked `private`",
    "Every field in a `private` block is already private. Remove the extra\n"
    "`private` on the field.")
N00B_DIAG(LOOP_NAME_BINDS_WHOLE_ITEM, "N00B-N0511", WARNING,
    "a single loop name does not match a field of the item, so it binds the whole item",
    "When a loop names one binding and the items are records, the name is\n"
    "matched against the item's fields. A name that matches no field binds\n"
    "the whole item instead; write `let` before it to say so:\n"
    "    for let entry in entries { ... }")
N00B_DIAG(TYPECASE_NAME_CLASH, "N00B-N0512", ERROR,
    "a `typecase` arm declares the name it narrows",
    "Inside a `typecase` arm the subject's name already refers to the\n"
    "narrowed value. Declaring that name again in the arm would hide it;\n"
    "use a different name.")
N00B_DIAG(UNKNOWN_LITERAL_MODIFIER, "N00B-N0513", ERROR,
    "no visible literal modifier handles this kind of literal",
    "A literal modifier must be declared in this module or exported by an\n"
    "imported module, and must handle the kind of literal it follows.\n"
    "Declare it, import the module that exports it, or use another one.")
N00B_DIAG(AMBIGUOUS_LITERAL_MODIFIER, "N00B-N0514", ERROR,
    "more than one imported module exports the same literal modifier",
    "Two imported modules export a literal modifier with this name for the\n"
    "same kind of literal, so the use is ambiguous. Import only one of\n"
    "them, or alias one modifier under another name.")
N00B_DIAG(LITERAL_MODIFIER_CLASH, "N00B-N0515", ERROR,
    "a literal modifier is declared with a name that is already in use",
    "A literal modifier name can refer to only one modifier for each kind\n"
    "of literal in a module, including modifiers that imports make\n"
    "visible. Choose a different name.")
N00B_DIAG(LITERAL_MODIFIER_ALIAS_UNKNOWN, "N00B-N0516", ERROR,
    "a literal modifier alias refers to a modifier that is not visible",
    "An alias for a literal modifier must name a modifier that is declared\n"
    "in this module or exported by an imported module.")
N00B_DIAG(CONFLICTING_TYPE_DEFINITION, "N00B-N0517", ERROR,
    "one type name is given two different definitions",
    "A type is defined once. Rename one of the definitions, or remove the\n"
    "duplicate.")
N00B_DIAG(COUNT_FIELD_UNKNOWN, "N00B-N0518", ERROR,
    "a `count` clause names a field the record does not have",
    "`count n` says another field of the same record holds the number of\n"
    "elements behind a `Foreign[...]` field. Name an existing integer field\n"
    "other than the pointer field itself.")
N00B_DIAG(UNION_BY_UNKNOWN_FIELD, "N00B-N0519", ERROR,
    "`union by` names something other than a plain field of the record",
    "`union by tag` selects the union arm using an integer field of the\n"
    "same record declared outside the union. Name such a field.")
N00B_DIAG(GENERIC_ARITY, "N00B-T0515", ERROR,
    "a generic type is given the wrong number of type arguments",
    "A generic type takes exactly the type arguments its declaration lists:\n"
    "    var items: List[int] = []\n"
    "    var table: Dict[string, int] = {:}")
N00B_DIAG(OPTION_USED_AS_VALUE, "N00B-T0516", ERROR,
    "an option that may be nil is used where its value is needed",
    "A value of type `T?` may be nil, so operators cannot use it directly.\n"
    "Test the variable against nil; where the test holds, the variable is a\n"
    "plain `T` until it is assigned again:\n"
    "    if v != nil {\n"
    "        total = v + 1\n"
    "    }")
N00B_DIAG(OPTION_COMPARED_WITH_VALUE, "N00B-T0517", ERROR,
    "an option is compared with something other than nil",
    "An option can only be compared with `nil`. Check it against nil first,\n"
    "then compare its value.")
N00B_DIAG(OPERATOR_OPERANDS_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0518", ERROR,
    "a binary operator is applied to operands of different types",
    "Arithmetic, bitwise and comparison operators need both operands to have\n"
    "the same type. Convert one operand so the types match.")
N00B_DIAG(OPERATOR_OPERAND_TYPE, "N00B-T0519", ERROR,
    "an operator is applied to a value of a type it does not support",
    "Each built-in operator works on particular types: `~` on integers and\n"
    "flagsets, unary `+` on numbers. Use an operand of a supported type.")
N00B_DIAG(OPERATOR_RESULT_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0520", ERROR,
    "an operator's result is used as a different type",
    "The result of an operator has a fixed type, such as `bool` for a\n"
    "comparison. It cannot be used where a different type is expected.")
N00B_DIAG(SHIFT_SIGNED_OPERAND, "N00B-T0521", ERROR,
    "a value that can be negative is shifted",
    "The built-in shifts work on unsigned integers and `bits` values.\n"
    "Convert a signed value to an unsigned type before shifting it.")
N00B_DIAG(SHIFT_COUNT_RANGE, "N00B-T0522", ERROR,
    "a shift count is negative or not smaller than the width of the value",
    "A value with N bits can be shifted by 0 to N-1 places. A larger or\n"
    "negative count is an error when it is known at compile time.")
N00B_DIAG(SHIFT_COUNT_SIGNED, "N00B-T0523", ERROR,
    "a shift count has a signed type",
    "Shift counts must have an unsigned type. Convert the count first.")
N00B_DIAG(INTEGER_CONSTANT_RANGE, "N00B-T0524", ERROR,
    "an integer constant does not fit the type it is used as",
    "A constant must lie within the range of the integer type it is given.\n"
    "Use a wider type or a smaller value:\n"
    "    let small: u8 = 255")
N00B_DIAG(INTEGER_NARROWING, "N00B-T0525", WARNING,
    "an integer conversion may receive values that do not fit",
    "The compiler could not prove every value fits the target type. If a\n"
    "value does not fit when the program runs, it stops with a panic.\n"
    "Check the value first, or use a wider type.")
N00B_DIAG(INTEGER_TOO_LARGE, "N00B-T0526", ERROR,
    "no integer type can hold every value an integer can have",
    "Integer values are limited to 128 bits. Give the value an explicit\n"
    "type or keep its range within what an integer type can hold.")
N00B_DIAG(BITWISE_NEGATIVE, "N00B-T0527", ERROR,
    "a value used with bitwise operators can be negative",
    "Bitwise operators work on unsigned integers, so a value used with them\n"
    "needs an unsigned type and cannot hold negative values.")
N00B_DIAG(CONSTANT_ZERO_DIVISOR, "N00B-T0528", ERROR,
    "a division or remainder has a divisor that is always zero",
    "Dividing by zero is never valid. Use a nonzero divisor.")
N00B_DIAG(STRING_NOT_BUFFER, "N00B-T0529", ERROR,
    "a string is used where a Buffer is required",
    "A string is immutable and does not convert to a Buffer. Copy it:\n"
    "    let b = buffer_from_string(s)")
N00B_DIAG(LITERAL_ITEM_TYPE_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0530", ERROR,
    "the items of a list, set or dict literal have different types",
    "All items of a container literal must share one type. Convert the item\n"
    "that differs, or give the container an explicit item type.")
N00B_DIAG(LITERAL_ITEMS_DO_NOT_FIT, "N00B-T0531", ERROR,
    "the items of a literal do not fit the type it builds",
    "A literal built by a literal modifier must have items the modifier can\n"
    "accept for the type it produces.")
N00B_DIAG(EMPTY_BRACES_AMBIGUOUS, "N00B-T0532", ERROR,
    "an empty `{}` could be a set or a dict",
    "Nothing says whether an empty `{}` is a set or a dict. Give the\n"
    "variable a type, or write `{:}` for an empty dict.")
N00B_DIAG(SHAPE_LITERAL_DEFAULT_CONFLICT, "N00B-T0533", ERROR,
    "a literal's default type conflicts with how it is used",
    "A literal with no other type information gets a default type, such as\n"
    "`List` for `[...]`. If it is then used as a different type, give it\n"
    "that type explicitly.")
N00B_DIAG(SHAPE_LITERAL_NO_HANDLER, "N00B-T0534", ERROR,
    "no literal modifier can build the expected type from this literal",
    "A literal used as a type other than its default is built by a literal\n"
    "modifier for that type. None is visible here; import one, or build the\n"
    "value another way.")
N00B_DIAG(SHAPE_LITERAL_AMBIGUOUS_HANDLER, "N00B-T0535", ERROR,
    "several literal modifiers can build the expected type from this literal",
    "More than one visible literal modifier produces the expected type. Name\n"
    "the one you mean after the literal.")
N00B_DIAG(LITERAL_MODIFIER_SIGNATURE, "N00B-T0536", ERROR,
    "a literal modifier is declared with the wrong signature",
    "A literal modifier takes the literal as its one typed parameter (a\n"
    "fence may add `site: Literal_Site`), returns the value it builds, and\n"
    "declares `fail: string`.")
N00B_DIAG(LOOP_BINDINGS_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0537", ERROR,
    "the names in a `for` loop do not match the shape of its items",
    "Loop names bind the positions of tuple items in order, or the fields of\n"
    "record items by name. A single name binds the whole item.")
N00B_DIAG(NOT_ITERABLE, "N00B-T0538", ERROR,
    "a `for` loop iterates over a value that cannot be iterated",
    "A `for` loop needs a value whose type implements the `Iterable` trait,\n"
    "such as a list or a range.")
N00B_DIAG(CALLBACK_NOT_A_CONTRACT, "N00B-T0539", ERROR,
    "`callback[...]` names a type that is not a callback type",
    "`callback[T](...)` creates a callback of a type declared with\n"
    "`callback`, which lists its `call`, `handler` and `setup` roles.")
N00B_DIAG(CALLBACK_STATE_NOT_WRITABLE, "N00B-T0540", ERROR,
    "the state given to a callback cannot be written",
    "A stateful callback updates its state, so the state must be declared\n"
    "with `var`.")
N00B_DIAG(CALLBACK_STATE_UNINITIALIZED, "N00B-T0541", ERROR,
    "the state given to a callback is not initialized",
    "A callback's state must hold a value before the callback is created.")
N00B_DIAG(CALLBACK_ARGUMENTS_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0542", ERROR,
    "the arguments to `callback[...]` do not match its handler and setup",
    "`callback[T](handler)` takes a handler matching the `handler` role, and\n"
    "for a stateful callback the state and the remaining `setup` arguments.")
N00B_DIAG(CALLBACK_TYPE_UNDETERMINED, "N00B-T0543", ERROR,
    "the arguments to `callback[...]` leave type parameters undetermined",
    "Every type parameter of a generic callback type must be fixed by the\n"
    "handler or state, or written explicitly.")
N00B_DIAG(CALLBACK_ROLES_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0544", ERROR,
    "the roles of a callback declaration do not fit together",
    "A callback has a `call` and a `handler` role. The handler takes the\n"
    "call's parameters, after a `modify` state when there is a `setup`\n"
    "role; `setup` takes references to the handler and the state.")
N00B_DIAG(CONFLICTING_RETURNS, "N00B-T0545", ERROR,
    "the return statements of a function produce different types",
    "Without a declared return type, every `return` in a function must\n"
    "produce the same type. Declare the return type, or make the returns\n"
    "agree.")
N00B_DIAG(FUNCTION_BODY_SIGNATURE_MISMATCH, "N00B-T0546", ERROR,
    "a function body returns or fails with a type its declaration does not allow",
    "The values a function returns, and the failures it raises, must match\n"
    "the return and `fail:` types in its declaration.")
N00B_DIAG(PARAMETER_TYPE_CONFLICT, "N00B-T0547", ERROR,
    "a parameter's declared type conflicts with another type it is given",
    "A parameter has one type. Its declared type must agree with its\n"
    "default value and with other declarations of the same function.")
N00B_DIAG(INIT_RECEIVER, "N00B-T0548", ERROR,
    "`__init` does not take the constructed value as its first parameter",
    "An `__init` function receives the value being constructed as its first\n"
    "parameter: `modify self: T` for a record, `self: T` or `modify self: T`\n"
    "for an object.")
N00B_DIAG(INIT_ON_VARIANT, "N00B-T0549", ERROR,
    "a variant type declares `__init`",
    "Variants are constructed by selecting an arm and giving its payload, so\n"
    "they cannot declare `__init`. Initialize the arm's payload type instead.")
N00B_DIAG(INIT_CANNOT_FAIL, "N00B-T0550", ERROR,
    "`__init` declares or raises a failure",
    "Construction cannot fail. Write a factory function that can fail and\n"
    "returns the constructed value instead.")
N00B_DIAG(INIT_RETURNS_VALUE, "N00B-T0551", ERROR,
    "`__init` returns a value",
    "`__init` fills in the value it receives and returns nothing. Use a\n"
    "factory function to produce a value.")
N00B_DIAG(FINALIZE_RECEIVER, "N00B-T0552", ERROR,
    "`__finalize` does not take one `consume` reference to the finalized value",
    "A finalizer takes exactly one parameter, a non-optional reference to\n"
    "the value being finalized, declared `consume`:\n"
    "    func __finalize(consume self: Ref[Handle]) { ... }")
N00B_DIAG(FINALIZE_CANNOT_FAIL, "N00B-T0553", ERROR,
    "`__finalize` declares or raises a failure",
    "A finalizer runs when a value is destroyed and has no caller to report\n"
    "to, so it cannot fail.")
N00B_DIAG(FINALIZE_RETURNS_VALUE, "N00B-T0554", ERROR,
    "`__finalize` returns a value",
    "A finalizer returns nothing.")
N00B_DIAG(CONTEXT_FAIL_WITHOUT_TYPE, "N00B-T0555", ERROR,
    "a context has a `fail` hook but no failure type",
    "A context's `fail` hook receives the context's failure value, so the\n"
    "context must declare `fail: T`. Add it, or remove the hook.")
N00B_DIAG(CONTEXT_HOOK_PARAMETER, "N00B-T0556", ERROR,
    "a context hook's parameter has a different type than the context gives it",
    "The `enter` hook's parameter receives the provided value and the `fail`\n"
    "hook's parameter the failure value; their declared types must match.")
N00B_DIAG(ARRAY_SIZE_NOT_POSITIVE, "N00B-T0557", ERROR,
    "an array size is zero or negative",
    "Each sized array dimension holds at least one element:\n"
    "    var cells: Array[int][16]")
N00B_DIAG(ARRAY_SIZED_AFTER_UNSIZED, "N00B-T0558", ERROR,
    "a sized array dimension follows an unsized one",
    "In an array type, sized dimensions come first and unsized ones last:\n"
    "    Array[int][4][]")
N00B_DIAG(ARRAY_SIZE_NOT_INTEGER, "N00B-T0559", ERROR,
    "an array size is not an integer",
    "Array dimensions are integer constants or integer expressions.")
N00B_DIAG(ARRAY_TYPE_SYNTAX, "N00B-T0560", ERROR,
    "array dimensions follow something other than `Array[Element]`",
    "An array type names its element type first, then its sizes:\n"
    "    Array[Node][513]")
N00B_DIAG(SIZED_INTEGER_WIDTH, "N00B-T0561", ERROR,
    "a sized integer or `bits` type has a width outside 1..128",
    "`i:N`, `u:N` and `bits:N` take a width from 1 to 128.")
N00B_DIAG(NIL_UNION_ARM, "N00B-T0562", ERROR,
    "`nil` is written as an arm of a union type",
    "A union type cannot list `nil` as an arm. Write the type as an option,\n"
    "`T?`, to allow nil.")
N00B_DIAG(TYPECASE_SUBJECT, "N00B-T0563", ERROR,
    "a `typecase` subject is not a variable or parameter",
    "`typecase` narrows the type of a variable or parameter inside each arm,\n"
    "so its subject must be one. Store an expression in a variable first.")
N00B_DIAG(COMPOSITE_FLAGSET_WRITE, "N00B-T0564", WARNING,
    "a combined flagset member is assigned a boolean",
    "Assigning to a member that combines several flags sets or clears all\n"
    "of them at once. Assign the individual flags if that is not intended.")
N00B_DIAG(FLAGSET_PIPE_UNION, "N00B-T0565", WARNING,
    "`|` is used for a flagset union",
    "Flagset unions are written with `+`. `|` is still accepted while code\n"
    "migrates.")
N00B_DIAG(UNKNOWN_LAYOUT_POLICY, "N00B-T0566", ERROR,
    "`layout(...)` names a policy that does not exist",
    "Record layout policies are `layout(c)` and `layout(ordered)`.")
N00B_DIAG(DUPLICATE_LAYOUT_MODIFIER, "N00B-T0567", ERROR,
    "a record has two layout policies or two alignments",
    "A record takes at most one `layout(...)` and one `align(...)`.")
N00B_DIAG(LAYOUT_MODIFIER_UNSUPPORTED, "N00B-T0568", ERROR,
    "a record layout modifier is not supported yet for the target",
    "`align(...)` and `layout(ordered)` are not supported yet for every\n"
    "target. Use `layout(c)` or remove the modifier.")
N00B_DIAG(C_LAYOUT_FIELD_TYPE, "N00B-T0569", ERROR,
    "a field of a `layout(c)` record has a type with no C representation",
    "Fields of a `layout(c)` record must have C-compatible types: sized\n"
    "integers, floats, `Foreign[...]` pointers and other `layout(c)`\n"
