N00B_DIAG(RECORD_MULTIPLE_UNIONS, "N00B-T0571", ERROR,
    "a record holds more than one union",
    "A record holds at most one union. Merge the arms into one union.")
N00B_DIAG(UNION_ARM_VALUE_NOT_CONSTANT, "N00B-T0572", ERROR,
    "a union arm's tag value is not a constant integer",
    "Each union arm is selected by a constant integer tag value.")
N00B_DIAG(UNION_ARM_DUPLICATE_VALUE, "N00B-T0573", ERROR,
    "two union arms have the same tag value",
    "Each arm of a union needs a distinct tag value.")
N00B_DIAG(UNTIL_SENTINEL_NOT_CONSTANT, "N00B-T0574", ERROR,
    "an `until` sentinel is not a constant integer",
    "`until v` ends a `Foreign[...]` sequence at the first element equal to\n"
    "v, so v must be a constant integer.")
N00B_DIAG(EXTENT_ON_NON_FOREIGN_FIELD, "N00B-T0575", ERROR,
    "an `until` or `count` clause is attached to a field that is not a `Foreign` pointer",
    "`until` and `count` describe how many elements a `Foreign[...]` field\n"
    "points at, so they only apply to such fields.")
N00B_DIAG(TYPE_CONTAINS_ITSELF, "N00B-T0576", ERROR,
    "a type contains itself by value",
    "A value cannot contain a copy of itself. Break the cycle with a\n"
    "reference, such as a `Ref[...]` or option field, or make one of the\n"
    "types an `object`.")
N00B_DIAG(ATOMIC_UNSUPPORTED, "N00B-T0577", ERROR,
    "the target has no atomic operations for a type",
    "Atomic values must fit the atomic instructions of the target. Use a\n"
    "smaller element type, or protect the value with a lock.")
N00B_DIAG(TUPLE_FIELD_REPEATED, "N00B-T0578", ERROR,
    "a field tuple type names a field twice",
    "Each field of a field tuple has its own name:\n"
    "    var point: Tuple[x: int, y: int]")
N00B_DIAG(TUPLE_NAMED_ARGUMENTS, "N00B-T0579", ERROR,
    "a type other than Tuple is given named type arguments",
    "Only `Tuple` takes named elements, which make a field tuple:\n"
    "    var point: Tuple[x: int, y: int]\n"
    "Other generic types take their type arguments by position.")
N00B_DIAG(TUPLE_ONE_ELEMENT, "N00B-T0580", ERROR,
    "a positional tuple type has one element",
    "A value is its own one-tuple, so `(a)` and `a` are the same and\n"
    "`Tuple[T]` is just `T`. Write the element type alone:\n"
    "    var count: int")
N00B_DIAG(TUPLE_IMMUTABLE, "N00B-T0581", ERROR,
    "an element of a tuple is assigned",
    "Tuples are values that cannot change in place. Build a new tuple and\n"
    "assign it instead:\n"
    "    point = (x = 3, y = point.y)")
N00B_DIAG(TUPLE_INDEX_NOT_CONSTANT, "N00B-T0582", ERROR,
    "a tuple is indexed by a value that is not a compile-time constant",
    "The elements of a tuple can have different types, so the index has to\n"
    "be known when the program is compiled:\n"
    "    let pair = (1, \"one\")\n"
    "    let name = pair[1]")
N00B_DIAG(TUPLE_INDEX_RANGE, "N00B-T0583", ERROR,
    "a tuple index is out of range",
    "A tuple with n elements is indexed from 0 to n - 1.")
N00B_DIAG(TUPLE_CONSTRUCTOR, "N00B-T0584", ERROR,
    "a field tuple builds a type that defines a constructor",
    "A field tuple fills in a record or object field by field, which would\n"
    "skip its constructor. Call the constructor instead, or write\n"
    "`unsafe_cast[T](...)` when skipping it is intended.")
N00B_DIAG(TUPLE_CAST, "N00B-T0585", ERROR,
    "a tuple cast between incompatible shapes",
    "`cast[T]` converts between a field tuple and a record or object whose\n"
    "fields have the same names and compatible types, in either direction.\n"
    "A positional tuple never converts to a record or object.")
